            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>Air sealing beyond the % mentioned above will result in more significant savings. I believe an air change of 2 or better could be achieved resulting in much higher savings than shown here. </airSeal>
                <mainWalls>I recommend adding R-40 insulation to achieve a total of R-60 for the best results. This should be done with a Larson Truss system or exterior rigid Ruxol. </mainWalls>
                <ceilings>I would recommend removing the old insulatio then installing a 3" layer of spray foam for air sealing followed by an additional layer of blown insulation to achieve a total of R-80. </ceilings>
                <HeatingSystem>Upgrading the furnace to a high efficiency condensing unit will save around 10% on fuel costs. Installing an air source heat pump will have more significant savings.</HeatingSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
